### Tewe Movies API — run these top-to-bottom in Rider/VS/VS Code.
### `login` and `createMovie` are named so later requests reuse the token and the new movie id.
### Start the stack first (./scripts/stack-up.sh) so the API (5001) and Identity (5003) are up.

@apiHost = https://localhost:5001
@identityHost = https://localhost:5003
@apiKey = dev-api-key
# A TMDB-imported movie (has details). Any slug from "Get all movies" works.
@tmdbSlug = the-odyssey-2026

### Generate a JWT (admin + trusted so every endpoint is reachable).
# @name login
POST {{identityHost}}/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userid": "d8566de3-b1a6-4a9b-b842-8e3887a82e41",
  "email": "ada.lovelace@tewe.local",
  "customClaims": {
    "admin": true,
    "trusted_member": true
  }
}

### Reuse the token from the login response for every authenticated call below.
@token = {{login.response.body.$}}

### Create a movie (Trusted). Captures the new id for the requests that follow.
# @name createMovie
POST {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Synergized Zero-Latency Standardization",
  "yearOfRelease": 2023,
  "genres": [ "Comedy" ]
}

@movieId = {{createMovie.response.body.$.id}}
@movieSlug = {{createMovie.response.body.$.slug}}

### Get all movies (anonymous). Supports title / year / sortBy / page / pageSize.
### Each item has posterUrl (TMDB movies), but details is always null in the list, by design.
GET {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies?page=1&pageSize=10&sortBy=-yearOfRelease
Accept: application/json

### Get a single movie by id or slug (anonymous). This one was just created, so it's a manual
### movie: posterUrl and details are null.
GET {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies/{{movieId}}
Accept: application/json

### Get a TMDB movie with its details (anonymous). The response adds:
###   posterUrl
###   details: tmdbId, imdbId, overview, tagline, runtimeMinutes, backdropUrl,
###            trailer { site, key, name, url, embedUrl },
###            directors / writers (role = job) / cast (top 10, role = character), each with profileUrl
GET {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies/{{tmdbSlug}}
Accept: application/json

### Update the movie (Trusted).
PUT {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies/{{movieId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Synergized Zero-Latency Standardization",
  "yearOfRelease": 2023,
  "genres": [ "Comedy", "Action" ]
}

### Rate the movie 1-5 (any authenticated user).
PUT {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies/{{movieId}}/ratings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "rating": 5
}

### List the current user's ratings.
GET {{apiHost}}/api/v1/ratings/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remove this user's rating for the movie.
DELETE {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies/{{movieId}}/ratings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete the movie (Admin).
DELETE {{apiHost}}/api/v1/movies/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Evict the "movies" output cache (API-key protected, no JWT).
POST {{apiHost}}/api/v1/admin/cache/evict
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
